From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:15:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 70/73] backends: let virtual input devices act as pens

Add clutter_virtual_input_device_notify_tablet_proximity(),
notify_tablet_motion() and notify_tablet_button(), implemented by the
native backend. A virtual tablet device brings a pen, an eraser or any
other tool near, moves it in stage coordinates with a pressure, and
presses its tip and buttons through the same paths a real tablet's
events take, so its tools follow the stylus settings, reach Wayland
clients through the tablet protocol and get their own cursor. Programs
that drive the desktop, such as Kestrel's checks, can write and hover
with a pen.

Upstream-Status: forwardable
